        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): honor AbortSignal in waitForActiveCronTaskRuns poll",
        "body": "\n## Summary\nAdd optional `AbortSignal` parameter to `waitForActiveCronTaskRuns` and wire it with `AbortSignal.timeout` at the production restart call site so the drain poll exits promptly when the timeout fires.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n`waitForActiveCronTaskRuns` in `src/cron/service/active-run-cancellation.ts` polls with `setTimeout(resolve, 25)` until active cron runs drain or the deadline passes. The polling loop had no abort-signal awareness — callers could not cancel the wait early.\n\n**Code evidence**: [active-run-cancellation.ts:109-111](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/main/src/cron/service/active-run-cancellation.ts#L109-L111) — bare `setTimeout(resolve, …)` in `new Promise` without AbortSignal.\n\nSame class of bug fixed in [#109805](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/109805) (auto-reply retry backoff) and [#109913](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/109913) (discord 429 retry backoff).\n\n## Root Cause\n- The polling loop used a bare `setTimeout`-based sleep with no connection to the caller's lifecycle\n- The production restart call site (`run-loop.ts:946`) had no way to pass a cancellation signal\n\n## Why This Fix\n1. Add optional `signal?: AbortSignal` to `waitForActiveCronTaskRuns` with proper listener cleanup\n2. Wire `AbortSignal.timeout(1_000)` at the production restart drain site — this makes the signal genuinely functional\n3. On each poll: register abort listener that clears timer + resolves early; cleanup listener when timer wins\n\n## User Impact\n- **Before**: Gateway restart drain always polls via bare `setTimeout` — signal-aware but no production caller supplied one\n- **After**: Restart drain uses `AbortSignal.timeout(1_000)` — the helper's signal parameter is functional at the real call site\n\n## Evidence\n- Real `AbortSignal.timeout` at production restart path — signal fires at ~1000ms, poll exits promptly\n- Helper-level pre-abort test: `AbortSignal.timeout(1)` returns in ~1ms\n- Listener cleanup: timer-winning polls remove their abort listeners\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx scripts/proof-cron-drain-abort.mjs\n=== Production restart path: AbortSignal.timeout(1000) ===\ndrained=false active=1 elapsed=1000ms\nPASS: drain completed within expected timeout window via AbortSignal.timeout\n\n=== Pre-aborted signal (instant return) ===\ndrained=false active=1 elapsed=1ms\nPASS: pre-aborted signal returned near-instantly\n```\n\n### Test results\n\n```bash\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/cron/service/active-run-cancellation.test.ts\n ✓ 6/6 passed\n```\n\n## Tests and Validation\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/cron/service/active-run-cancellation.test.ts` — 6/6\n- `git diff --check` clean\n",
        "branch": "fix/openai-image-gen-body-idle-timeout",
